  "Question": "If \\(x\\lt0,\\) then \\(\\left|x-\\sqrt{(x-1)^2}\\right|\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(1-2x\\)",
    "C": "\\(-2x-1\\)",
    "D": "\\(1+2x\\)",
    "E": "\\(2x-1\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The square root symbol gives the nonnegative root, so \\(\\sqrt{u^2}=|u|\\). Since \\(x<0\\), we have \\(x-1<0\\), giving\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(x-1)^2}=|x-1|=1-x.\n\\]\nTherefore the expression is\n\\[\n\\left|x-(1-x)\\right|=|2x-1|.\n\\]\nBecause \\(2x-1<0\\), its absolute value is \\(-(2x-1)=1-2x\\). The answer is \\(\\boxed{1-2x}\\), choice B.",
